    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the whole suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment (`<LAST3>-<NNNN>`) with minimal structural impact \u2014 small, cohesive additions rather than growing any existing method or class.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`util/CustomerCode.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny, self-contained helper (`WMC_other = 0`, `CC = 1`) that formats the code: upper-cased first three letters of the last name, a dash, and a 4-digit zero-padded sequence one greater than the current owner count.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column`) plus a plain getter/setter so the value is durable and MapStruct/JPA can carry it.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema. The generated `OwnerDto` picks it up, and MapStruct maps it by name automatically \u2014 so no change to `OwnerMapper` was needed.\n\n4. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 one added line in `addOwner` assigns the code at creation time (using the live owner count), so the sequence is fixed when the owner is created and stays stable on later reads.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column. This is the test DB (`ddl-auto=none`); the other profiles already rely on `ddl-auto=update` and omit optional columns (e.g. `registration_date`), so I matched that existing pattern rather than touching them.\n\nThe single acceptance test verifies both the `SMI-`/`JON-` prefix format and that the global sequence increments by exactly 1 between consecutive creations \u2014 both now pass.",
